== Availability

By design, a failed task, a broker outage or an identity outage loses no committed payment or event (AD-04, AD-06). Qualified AWS V5/V7 passes and the new 15 November focused payment-initiation failure/recovery result partially resolve AISS-13, not the original broader webhook drill or whole campaign. The historical 13 November identity R1 remains failed. The database, the Valkey node and the NAT instance each run in one zone, so a zone failure still stops purchases, sign-ins or outbound calls (AISS-01). @tbl-availability-failures lists each failure, what recovers it and whether we saw it on AWS or locally.

*Application recovery.* On 16 October on AWS, two healthy commerce tasks ran in different zones. That deployment passed its smoke suite at 14:10 SGT only after an interrupted start and a manual repair of suspended scaling targets (#src("docs/swe5001/evidence/20261016-http-baseline-dashboard/README.md")[placement record], AISS-14). The ALB routes only to healthy targets, and ECS keeps the desired task count (AD-07, AD-08). The deployment circuit breaker rolls an unhealthy deployment back to the last completed one (#src("infra/swe5001/modules/ecs-service/main.tf")[ECS service module]). V5's controlled result follows. Configured, not tested: V6 (a bad release rolled back) was not run on AWS.

*V5 controlled task replacement.* On 13 November 2026 on AWS, V5 R3 passed: *60,000 workload GETs* plus one setup GET, with zero invalid/non-2xx responses, browse errors or dropped iterations. After the approved task stop under load, the first source-bound ALB-healthy observation was at *79.458 s*, within the unchanged *120 s* limit; this is an observation time, not an exact health-transition instant. The tested correction was commerce *1,024 CPU units / 2,048 MiB*, a pool of *five* connections and *120 s* ALB slow start; it does not pass R2's smaller configuration, whose errors and *155 s* replacement failure remain retained. R1's interrupted workload also remains failed. V5 used released application `3a893036` with separately recorded tooling and runtime corrections, not the later experimental V4 R5 image. Source: #published-evidence("20261114-v4-r5-live/v5-r3-pass.md")[published V5 R3 record]; §2.2 explains the PR publication boundary.

